{"t":{"t":10,"i":0,"p":{"k":["result","context"],"v":[{"t":10,"i":1,"p":{"k":["type","title","description","props"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"openapi"},{"t":1,"s":"Create Event Based Addon"},{"t":1,"s":"Creates an event-based addon definition under the specified product lineup. An event-based addon can then be added and “provisioned” for a subscription.\\n\\nEvent-based addons are similar to other addon types, in that you define the addon parameters (such as name and taxability) and the pricing. A key difference for the event-based addon is that it must be attached to a metric. This is because the metric provides the addon with the actual quantity used in computing what and how much will be billed each period for each subscription.\\n\\nSo, instead of reporting usage directly for each addon (as you would with metered addons), the usage is derived from analysis of your events.\\n\\nFor more information on addons, see our documentation here.\\n\\nIf you have the new Catalog experience enabled, taxable addons must include a non-blank `tax_code`. Sending `\\\"tax_code\\\": \\\"\\\"` returns `422`."},{"t":10,"i":2,"p":{"k":["payload","document","operations","showDescription"],"v":[{"t":10,"i":3,"p":{"k":["bundled","proxyUrl"],"v":[{"t":10,"i":4,"p":{"k":["openapi","info","tags","servers","security","paths","components"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"3.2.0"},{"t":10,"i":5,"p":{"k":["title","version","contact","description","x-server-configuration"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"Ombrevix Billing"},{"t":1,"s":"1.0"},{"t":10,"i":6,"p":{"k":["email"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"support@ombrevix.example"}]},"o":0},{"t":1,"s":"\\nOmbrevix Billing provides an HTTP-based API that conforms to the principles of REST.\\nOne of the many reasons to use Ombrevix Billing is the immense feature set and client libraries.\\nThe Ombrevix API returns JSON responses as the primary and recommended format, but XML is also provided as a backwards compatible option for merchants who require it.\\n\\n## Steps to make your first Ombrevix Billing API call\\n\\n1. Sign-up or log-in to your test workspace account.\\n2. Setup authentication credentials.\\n3. Submit an API request and verify the response.\\n5. Test the Ombrevix Billing integrations.\\n\\nNext, you can explore authentication methods, basic concepts for interacting with Ombrevix Billing via the API, and the entire set of application-based documentation to aid in your discovery of the product.\\n\\n### Request Example\\n\\nThe following example uses the curl command-line tool to make an API request.\\n\\n**Request**\\n\\n    curl -u \\x3Capi_key>:x -H Accept:application/json -H Content-Type:application/json https://acme.ombrevix.example/subscriptions"},{"t":10,"i":7,"p":{"k":["default-server","default-environment","environments","parameters"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"production"},{"t":1,"s":"US"},{"t":9,"i":8,"a":[{"t":10,"i":9,"p":{"k":["name","description","servers"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"US"},{"t":1,"s":"Default Ombrevix Billing environment hosted in US. Valid for the majority of our customers."},{"t":9,"i":10,"a":[{"t":10,"i":11,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://{workspace}.ombrevix.example"},{"t":1,"s":"production"}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":12,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://events.ombrevix.example/{workspace}"},{"t":1,"s":"ebb"}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":13,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://{connector}.api.ombrevix.example"},{"t":1,"s":"oauth"}]},"o":0}],"o":0}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":14,"p":{"k":["name","description","servers"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"EU"},{"t":1,"s":"Ombrevix Billing environment hosted in EU. Use only when you requested EU hosting for your AB account."},{"t":9,"i":15,"a":[{"t":10,"i":16,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://{workspace}.eu.ombrevix.example"},{"t":1,"s":"production"}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":17,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://{connector}.api.ombrevix.example"},{"t":1,"s":"oauth"}]},"o":0}],"o":0}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":18,"p":{"k":["name","description","servers"],"v":[{